  "description": "disk add writes a disk's marker and records it seen. A filesystem with its identifier and none of its marker, as a clone made before disk add, mounted in its place, is then missing, no-marker, at the check of the next pass, and in disk list: it is not walked and nothing is written to it, and the file waits degraded. disk mark without --yes, and with --dry-run, say what they would write; with --yes the marker is written again as disk add writes it, and the next pass copies the file. A disk that holds its own marker is nothing to do, and catalog rebuild records each disk's own marker seen again.",
